• volatility in our share price, which may lead to higher stock-based compensation expense;
• volatility in our effective tax rate;
• general socioeconomic and political conditions in the countries where we operate or where our products are sold or used, including the
COVID-19 pandemic, U.S.-China relations and the conditions in Hong Kong; and
• costs associated with litigation, especially related to intellectual property.
